35:["$","details","ts-p3",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",3]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"How does the difference in structure change what each text is able to do?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"B. Text A explains how the backlog developed, while Text B evaluates options for reducing it — so Text A supplies the cause that Text B's solutions have to address."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"Structure determines usefulness. A chronology shows origins; a problem/solution weighs responses. Read together, Text A explains why Text B's third option is the one that addresses the actual cause."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Text A proves the backlog is unsolvable, while Text B proves it is easy to solve."}]," ","— ","Neither text claims either thing. Text B's last sentence says partial measures help but do not eliminate the problem."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Text A explains how the backlog developed, while Text B evaluates options for reducing it — so Text A supplies the cause that Text B's solutions have to address."}]," ","— ","Correct. It names both structures accurately and explains what each one makes possible."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Both texts are organized the same way, so neither adds anything the other lacks."}]," ","— ","The two structures are clearly different — dates versus proposed responses."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Text A is opinion and Text B is fact."}]," ","— ","Both texts are informational. Neither is presented as the author's opinion."]}]]}]]]}]]}]
36:["$","section","ts-challenge",{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-3 font-display text-lg font-bold text-eng-navy-900","children":"Challenge"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","details","ts-c1",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",1]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"Which best describes the overall structure of the passage?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"C. Compare and contrast — it sets two timekeeping systems side by side on the same points and concludes that each fails in a different way"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"Paragraph 1 is a short timeline that sets up the change, but from paragraph 2 on, every paragraph weighs paper against the app: who creates the record, which is better at arithmetic, which creates new disputes. Paragraph 5 closes the comparison by naming how each system fails. That shape holds from the second paragraph to the last, so it is the structure of the whole."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Chronology — it traces the warehouse's move from paper timesheets to an app, in the order events happened"}]," ","— ","This describes paragraph 1 only. After the switch is introduced, no more events happen — the rest of the passage compares the two systems."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Problem and solution — it presents the disputes over hours and shows how the app solved them"}]," ","— ","Paragraph 1 raises this possibility and rejects it in the same breath: \"It did not settle them. It moved them.\" The passage never presents the app as the fix."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Compare and contrast — it sets two timekeeping systems side by side on the same points and concludes that each fails in a different way"}]," ","— ","Correct. Two systems, compared on matching points, with a conclusion that weighs both. This is the structure that organizes the whole passage."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],"$L3b"," ","— ","This describes one sentence in paragraph 3. It is a smaller pattern nested inside the comparison, not the shape of the passage."]}]]}]]]}]]}],"$L3c","$L3d","$L3e"]}]]}]
37:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 border-t border-eng-navy-100 pt-3 text-xs italic text-eng-navy-400","children":"Original passage — BEOC Academic Bridge"}]
38:["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","$L2a","ts-m1",{"question":{"id":"ts-m1","type":"multiple-choice","question":"In Passage 1, the words First, Next, Then, and Finally signal which structure?","passageId":"ts-mastery-p1","choices":["Chronology / sequence","Compare and contrast","Cause and effect","Description"],"correctAnswer":0,"explanation":"First, next, then, and finally are the core sequence signal words. Four of them from one family settles the structure. If you missed this, revisit the signal-word table at the top of the lesson.","choiceRationales":["Correct. Four sequence signals, and the steps are meant to be followed in order.","Nothing is compared. There is one process, described step by step.","Cause-and-effect signals such as because or as a result do not organize this passage.","Description has no required order. This passage says the order itself matters."],"skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"Foundation"},"number":1}],["$","$L2a","ts-m2",{"question":{"id":"ts-m2","type":"multiple-choice","question":"What is the structure of Passage 2?","passageId":"ts-mastery-p2","choices":["Problem and solution — it identifies unreported injuries and explains how to fix the problem","Cause and effect — it explains why injuries go unreported and what happens as a result","Chronology — it lists the steps for reporting an injury in order","Compare and contrast — it compares minor injuries with serious ones"],"correctAnswer":1,"explanation":"\"Because\" and \"as a result\" are cause-and-effect signals, and the passage ends on a consequence — a claim that becomes hard to prove. No one does anything about the problem. If you chose problem and solution, revisit the test tip in the lesson: if no one responds to the problem, it is cause and effect.","choiceRationales":["The passage names a problem, but it never proposes a fix. It ends on a consequence, not a response.","Correct. Reasons (causes) lead to an unrecorded injury and a weaker claim (effects).","Passage 2 contains no steps. Passage 1 is the one that lists them.","Minor and serious injuries are never set side by side. The strain that \"turns out to be more serious\" is an effect, not a point of comparison."],"skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"Developing"},"number":2}],["$","$L2a","ts-m3",{"question":{"id":"ts-m3","type":"multiple-choice","question":"Why does the author of Passage 1 most likely use a sequence structure?","passageId":"ts-mastery-p1","choices":["To tell the story of one worker's injury in the order it happened","Because the steps work best in a particular order, and the passage is written to help the reader act","To compare the reporting deadlines used in different states","Because every workplace document is written as a sequence"],"correctAnswer":1,"explanation":"The first sentence states the reason outright: \"the order in which you act matters.\" The author wants the reader to do something, and sequence is the structure that fits instructions. If you missed this, revisit \"Structure follows purpose\" in the lesson.","choiceRationales":["No single worker appears. The passage speaks to \"you,\" the reader, which is how instructions are written.","Correct. Structure follows purpose: order matters here, so the author uses sequence.","State deadlines are mentioned once, in the last sentence, and are not compared.","This is outside knowledge, and it is not true. The answer has to come from this passage."],"skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"TABE Ready"},"number":3}],"$L3f"]}]
3a:["$","$L2a","ts-c4",{"question":{"id":"ts-c4","type":"short-response","question":"The author could have told this as a simple timeline: paper first, then the app. In three or four sentences, name the structure the author used instead, quote two signal words or phrases that show it, and explain what that structure lets the author say that a timeline would not.","passageId":"ts-challenge-clock","explanation":"A complete answer does three jobs: it names the structure, quotes signal words that prove it, and connects the structure to what the author is trying to say. The third job is the one most answers leave out — and it is the one that shows you understand why structure matters.","sampleResponse":"The passage is organized as compare and contrast. Phrases such as \"The two systems differ first in\" and \"Whereas a forgotten entry on paper\" set paper timesheets and the app side by side on the same points. A timeline would only show that the warehouse switched from one system to the other, which would make the app look like the solution. Comparing the two directly lets the author show that each system fails in its own way — paper through arithmetic errors, the app through missing entries — which is the point of the final paragraph.","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":"Challenge"},"number":4}]
3b:["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"Cause and effect — it explains how the app caused the payroll clerk's workload to drop"}]
3c:["$","details","ts-c2",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",2]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"How does paragraph 4 relate to paragraph 3?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"B. It presents a drawback of the app that balances the advantage described in paragraph 3."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"Paragraph 3 credits the app with ending arithmetic errors. Paragraph 4 opens with \"That same automation, however\" — a contrast signal — and shows the same feature creating new disputes. It is the other side of the comparison."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"It continues the timeline, describing what happened after the arithmetic errors disappeared."}]," ","— ","No time order connects the two paragraphs. \"However\" signals a contrast, not a next step."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"It presents a drawback of the app that balances the advantage described in paragraph 3."}]," ","— ","Correct. The advantage in paragraph 3 and the drawback in paragraph 4 are two sides of the same feature."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"It proposes a solution to the arithmetic errors described in paragraph 3."}]," ","— ","The arithmetic errors were already solved in paragraph 3. Paragraph 4 raises new problems rather than fixing old ones."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"It gives a second example of the same advantage described in paragraph 3."}]," ","— ","\"However\" marks a turn. Paragraph 4 argues against the app, not for it."]}]]}]]]}]]}]
3d:["$","details","ts-c3",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",3]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"Which phrases from the passage signal its overall structure? Select all that apply."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-green-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["Correct answer:"," "]}],"B. \"The two systems differ first in\" (paragraph 2)  •  D. \"Whereas a forgotten entry on paper\" (paragraph 4)  •  E. \"Neither system, in other words\" (paragraph 5)"]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"Three phrases set paper and the app against each other — \"differ,\" \"whereas,\" and \"neither system\" all belong to the comparison family. The other two are real signal words, but they signal the smaller structures nested inside the passage."]}],[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-2 mt-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-eng-navy-500","children":"Every choice, explained"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-2","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["A","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"\"For eleven years\" (paragraph 1)"}]," ","— ","A chronology signal, but it belongs to the setup in paragraph 1. It does not organize the rest of the passage."]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["B","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"\"The two systems differ first in\" (paragraph 2)"}]," ","— ","Correct. \"Differ\" announces a comparison, and \"first\" tells you more points of comparison are coming."]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-red-700","children":["C","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"\"Because the app calculates totals itself\" (paragraph 3)"}]," ","— ","A cause-and-effect signal inside a single paragraph. It explains one advantage; it does not organize the whole passage."]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["D","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"\"Whereas a forgotten entry on paper\" (paragraph 4)"}]," ","— ","Correct. \"Whereas\" sets the two systems directly against each other within one sentence."]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-700","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mr-1 font-bold text-eng-green-700","children":["E","."]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-eng-navy-500","children":"\"Neither system, in other words\" (paragraph 5)"}]," ","— ","Correct. \"Neither system\" only makes sense if two things have been compared, and it opens the concluding comparison."]}]]}]]]}]]}]
3e:["$","details","ts-c4",{"className":"group rounded-xl border border-eng-navy-200 bg-white","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start gap-3 rounded-xl p-4 font-medium text-eng-navy-900 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-eng-teal-600","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 shrink-0 rounded bg-eng-navy-100 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold text-eng-navy-700","children":["Q",4]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex-1 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed","children":"The author could have told this as a simple timeline: paper first, then the app. In three or four sentences, name the structure the author used instead, quote two signal words or phrases that show it, and explain what that structure lets the author say that a timeline would not."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"shrink-0 text-eng-navy-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180","aria-hidden":"true","children":"▾"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-eng-navy-100 p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-3 rounded-lg bg-eng-teal-50 p-3 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-bold text-eng-teal-800","children":["Model response:"," "]}],"The passage is organized as compare and contrast. Phrases such as \"The two systems differ first in\" and \"Whereas a forgotten entry on paper\" set paper timesheets and the app side by side on the same points. A timeline would only show that the warehouse switched from one system to the other, which would make the app look like the solution. Comparing the two directly lets the author show that each system fails in its own way — paper through arithmetic errors, the app through missing entries — which is the point of the final paragraph."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-eng-navy-800","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold","children":"Why: "}],"A complete answer does 